  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nThe [internal ancestor origin objects list creation steps](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#internal-ancestor-origin-objects-list-creation-steps) start:\n\n> 1. Let _output_ be « ».\n> 2. Let _parentDoc_ be _document_'s container document.\n> 3. If _parentDoc_ is null, then return _output_.\n\nA document's container document goes through its node navigable, which is null until the document is some navigable's active document. Both callers run before that:\n\n- [create a new browsing context and document](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-sequences.html#creating-a-new-browsing-context), before the caller creates the navigable\n- [create and initialize a `Document` object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/document-lifecycle.html#initialise-the-document-object), before the navigation makes the new document active\n\nSo _parentDoc_ is always null and `location.ancestorOrigins` is always empty.\n\nMaybe the callers could pass in _parentDoc_: the embedder's node document for the initial `about:blank`, and _navigationParams_'s navigable's container document otherwise.\n\n(Found by @shannonbooth in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12572#issuecomment-5960317945.)\n",
